{"key": "55fd5a596eb3b39a109aafab125fb0073120a7e3cee8b697945a3b687b3cc9b7", "request_digest": "55fd5a596eb3b39a109aafab125fb0073120a7e3cee8b697945a3b687b3cc9b7", "response_json": {"container": null, "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"caller": {"type": "direct"}, "id": "toolu_011EXSf19ZoxWseJnvUPZck4", "input": {"edges": [{"dst": "fee_revenue", "identity": "fee_revenue = orders * fee_per_order", "rationale": "Accounting identity for a revenue-per-unit metric. validate_identity passed: 3360 observations, median and p95 residual 0.0, total max residual 1.8e-16. Written in product form as the rules require, not as fee_per_order = fee_revenue / orders.", "src": "orders", "type": "formula"}, {"dst": "fee_revenue", "identity": "fee_revenue = orders * fee_per_order", "rationale": "Second component of the same identity: fee revenue equals units ordered times fee per unit. Matches the SQL, SUM(fee_revenue)/SUM(units), which pools numerator and denominator.", "src": "fee_per_order", "type": "formula"}, {"dimension": "country", "dst": "fee_per_order", "rationale": "Declared dimension. validate_breakdown passed with pooled num/den: n=336, median and p95 residual 0.0.", "src": "fee_per_order", "type": "breakdown"}, {"dimension": "platform", "dst": "fee_per_order", "rationale": "Declared dimension. validate_breakdown passed: n=336, residual 0.0.", "src": "fee_per_order", "type": "breakdown"}, {"dimension": "category", "dst": "fee_per_order", "rationale": "Declared dimension. validate_breakdown passed: n=336, residual 0.0.", "src": "fee_per_order", "type": "breakdown"}, {"dimension": "seller_tier", "dst": "fee_per_order", "rationale": "Declared dimension. validate_breakdown passed: n=336, residual 0.0.", "src": "fee_per_order", "type": "breakdown"}, {"dimension": "channel", "dst": "fee_per_order", "rationale": "Declared dimension. validate_breakdown passed: n=336, residual 0.0.", "src": "fee_per_order", "type": "breakdown"}], "notes": "Placement: fee_per_order is fee revenue per unit ordered, so it is a revenue-per-unit metric, not a count rate. I placed it with the identity fee_revenue = orders * fee_per_order. That parallels the existing gmv = orders * aov. The identity passed at the total and at shared segments: n=3360, 672 skipped, median and p95 residual 0. Two full-combination segments had n=0 and are marked passed=false: DE/web/electronics/search/1P and FR/web/electronics/search/small_3P. Those combinations had no shared data, so the identity could not be tested there; nothing contradicted it. All 5 declared dimensions reconcile (country, platform, category, seller_tier, channel; each n=336, residual 0). No dimensions are missing compared with orders and fee_revenue. Refunds has no relationship to this metric.\n\nUnit: I inferred eur, meaning euros per unit. The contributor declared 'ratio', but the numerator is in euros and the description says euros per unit ordered. Values range from about 1.29 to 2.06 EUR per unit with a strong daily cycle, and the 14-day level drifts slightly down (daily peak 2.06 on Jan 15 vs 1.90 on Jan 28). The metadata also tags it domain 'quality'; it fits revenue/orders better.\n\nPossible duplicate: none. No existing metric computes fee_revenue/orders. aov is GMV per unit, a different numerator.\n\nCandidate cause not added: aov \u2192 fee_per_order. Because fees are charged on merchandise value, higher average selling price should push fees per unit up in the same hour. The data contradicts this. Deseasonalized first-difference correlation is NEGATIVE: -0.93 at lag 0 and -0.96 at lag 1. It then reverses sign with a roughly 24h period (+0.81 at lag 13, -0.93 at lag 24). That looks like leftover daily-cycle structure, not a same-hour positive fee mechanism. A plausible explanation is a mix shift: hours with higher AOV may come from lower-fee segments. I could not confirm this without segment-level fee rates. Correlation is not causation in either direction, so I left the causal edge out and flag it as undecided. lagged_correlation of fee_revenue \u2192 fee_per_order returned 0 usable points, so I could not measure that link (it is already covered by the identity).", "unit": "eur"}, "name": "submit", "toolset_name": null, "type": "tool_use"}], "context_management": null, "diagnostics": null, "id": "msg_011ChGM4XcHfLAPDsuJTu4ix", "input_transformations": null, "model": "claude-opus-5-5", "role": "assistant", "stop_details": null, "stop_reason": "tool_use", "stop_sequence": null, "type": "message", "usage": {"cache_creation": {"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0}, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 0, "cache_read_input_tokens": 2430, "fallback_credit": null, "inference_geo": "global", "input_tokens": 25435, "iterations": [{"cache_creation": {"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0}, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 0, "cache_read_input_tokens": 2430, "input_tokens": 25435, "model": null, "output_tokens": 1649, "type": "message"}], "output_tokens": 1649, "output_tokens_details": {"thinking_tokens": 125}, "server_tool_use": null, "service_tier": "standard", "speed": "standard"}}}
